The original package name `moe.shizuku.manager.adb` is preserved so that
attribution is visible in stack traces and in the source tree itself. These
files are not PhysiBoard's own work and are not covered by PhysiBoard's
licence; they carry Apache-2.0 and its terms travel with them.

`libadb.so` is a prebuilt native library from the same project.

PhysiBoard uses this to pair once with the phone's own Wireless Debugging, so
the keyboard can set the backlight and drive the notification ring without
requiring root or a separate app to be installed.

Upstream's own pairing SERVICE is deliberately not carried over. It existed to
drive a notification and a screen belonging to the app around it, which is
integration rather than protocol, so PhysiBoard 3.0 writes its own against the
pairing CLIENT here. What remains in this module is the ADB protocol, the key
handling, the discovery and the pairing client: the parts that are genuinely
third-party.

Modifications by PhysiBoard: AdbPairingService removed; AdbMdns logs its discovery and resolve verdicts at info level because the Titan drops verbose logs; AdbClient gained execWithInput, which writes a file to a command's standard input, so PhysiBoard can install its own update through `cmd package install -S`.
